course: dictionary
lesson: 6979
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Panther is a noun: a panther, panthers. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «A black panther is not a separate animal but a dark leopard or jaguar.» Here the clues are black and dark, so the panther is a big wild cat.
explain: Context works the same way in science and in stories. In a science text, «black panther» names a leopard or jaguar with a lot of dark colour. In a story, the panther Bagheera is wise and calm, so the word names a character. Ask yourself what the sentence is about, then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: Check your choice by putting the meaning into the sentence. If «a panther» means a big wild cat and the sentence still makes sense, you have it. «Florida panther» is different: in North America, the same word is another name for a puma or cougar. The place in the phrase is your clue.
fact: A panther is a big wild cat, usually a leopard or a jaguar with black fur.
fact: A «black panther» is a leopard or jaguar with extra dark colour, and its spots can still be seen in bright light.
fact: In North America, «panther» is another name for a puma or cougar, as in the «Florida panther».
fact: Panthers are carnivores, which means they eat meat, and they are skilled hunters.
fact: The panther Bagheera in «The Jungle Book» is wise and calm, and sports teams often use the name «Panthers».
exercise: «A black panther is not a separate animal but a dark leopard or jaguar.» What is a black panther? | A separate kind of animal with no spots | *A dark leopard or jaguar | A bird with black feathers | A cartoon cat
exercise: In North America, what is another name for a panther? | A wolf | A kind of tree | *A puma or cougar | A pink cartoon
exercise: Bagheera in «The Jungle Book» is wise and calm. What is Bagheera? | A sports team | *A panther | A bird | A cartoon
test: «In bright sunlight, you can still see the spots of a black panther.» What does this tell you? | It is a different kind of animal | *Its spots still show under the dark colour | Its spots have all disappeared | It only lives at night
test: Panthers are carnivores. What does carnivore mean? | A kind of cat food | *Meat-eater | Plant-eater | Fish-eater
exam: Which word means more than one panther? | panthern | *panthers | panther's | a panther
